&lt;p&gt;By harnessing AI, a unified platform, and an extensive partner ecosystem, we help customers turn compliance into a catalyst for growth, operational resilience, and enduring regulatory trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than 3,000 enterprises across 75 countries rely on our end-to-end platform and the world’s most comprehensive financial crime risk intelligence. With full-stack agentic automation, we help organizations automate up to 95% of KYC, AML, and sanctions reviews, cut onboarding times by 50%, reduce false positives by 70%, and handle 7x more work with the same staff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ComplyAdvantage is headquartered in London and has global hubs in New York, Lisbon, Singapore, and Cluj-Napoca. It is backed by Balderton Capital, Index Ventures, Ontario Teachers’ Pension Plan, Goldman Sachs, and Andreessen Horowitz. Learn more about compliance re-engineered for the age of AI at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://complyadvantage.com&quot;&gt;complyadvantage.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;","departments":[{"id":4044837002,"name":"Commercial","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4024097002,"name":"London, UK","location":"London, England, United Kingdom","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app2.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8902109002/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://complyadvantage.com/careers/jobs/8785705002?gh_jid=8785705002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":6514713002,"location":{"name":"London, England, United Kingdom"},"metadata":null,"id":8785705002,"updated_at":"2026-11-05T08:55:57-05:00","requisition_id":"206174","title":"Manager- Business Development","company_name":"ComplyAdvantage","first_published":"2026-09-14T04:25:32-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About ComplyAdvantage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ComplyAdvantage is the financial industry’s leading source of AI-driven financial crime risk data and detection technology. Our mission is to neutralize the risk of money laundering, terrorist financing, corruption, and other financial crimes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than 1,000 companies globally rely on us to navigate risk through the world’s only real-time database of people and companies. Backed by Goldman Sachs, Ontario Teachers’, Index Ventures, and Balderton Capital, we have raised over $100M to date. After growing our team by 40% last year, we are scaling from 500 to 600+ people - and our SDR team is the engine behind that growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a people-leadership role first. As Head of Business Development for EMEA, you own the outbound business development (BDR) function across the region — hiring, developing, and leading a team of BDRs whose job is to generate qualified pipeline for our new-business sales organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will set the outbound strategy, build the ramp and coaching systems that make reps successful, and create the career pathways that turn strong BDRs into future account executives. Your success is measured by the performance, retention, and progression of the team you build — and by the quality of pipeline they generate for the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and coach the team. Run daily coaching, call reviews, and 1:1s that raise the performance of every BDR — developing outbound craft, resilience, and commercial judgment across the group.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the hiring bar. Run a structured, competency-based interview process, and keep a bench of talent ahead of demand so the team can scale without dropping quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design onboarding and ramp. Build and run a structured 90-day onboarding program with clear milestone gates, so new hires reach full productivity faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build career pathways. Maintain a competency framework with assessable junior and senior behaviors, and create clear BDR-to-AE progression that helps you attract and retain ambitious reps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the outbound strategy. Define account prioritization, ideal-customer-profile targeting, messaging, and multi-channel sequencing across EMEA, in partnership with Sales and Marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own pipeline generation. Carry the team’s qualified-pipeline target, forecast opportunities into the new-business funnel, and use data to diagnose and fix what is not working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across the business. Work with Revenue Operations on tooling, routing, reporting, and compensation design, and align closely with Marketing on account-based programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on performance. Give sales leadership a clear, evidence-based view of team health, ramp, and pipeline contribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proficient with:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cognism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales Nav&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building multi-outreach&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Insights into performing channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;People-management experience is essential. We are looking for someone with a strong track record of managing an outbound BDR or SDR team — you have hired, coached, and retained reps and led a team to target, not only carried a number yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team leadership. Proven experience leading and developing outbound BDRs/SDRs, with a genuine interest in growing people and a record of moving reps into more senior roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building the function. Experience designing or scaling onboarding, ramp, coaching, and performance frameworks — not just running the ones you inherited.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outbound craft. Strong command of prospecting, multi-channel sequencing, and qualification (MEDDIC or a similar framework), with the ability to teach it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data fluency. Comfortable in Salesforce and reporting tools, using metrics to manage a team, forecast pipeline, and make decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial background. Experience selling or generating pipeline in B2B SaaS; exposure to RegTech, FinTech, financial services, or compliance is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The right blend. The emotional intelligence to develop people, and the operational rigor to run a team at scale across multiple markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice to have&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or managing teams across multiple EMEA markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with anti-money laundering (AML), sanctions, or wider financial crime compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Marketing on account-based experience (ABX) or account-based marketing (ABM) programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How we work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our values shape how this team operates, and we hire for them:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make a safer world. The work matters — we help stop the movement of funds that fuel serious crime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the bar. We hold a high standard for ourselves and each other, and we keep getting better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See it, own it, drive it forward. We take ownership and follow through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Win as one team. We succeed together, across functions and regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to empower every business to eliminate financial crime.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By harnessing AI, a unified platform, and an extensive partner ecosystem, we help customers turn compliance into a catalyst for growth, operational resilience, and enduring regulatory trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than 3,000 enterprises across 75 countries rely on our end-to-end platform and the world’s most comprehensive financial crime risk intelligence. With full-stack agentic automation, we help organizations automate up to 95% of KYC, AML, and sanctions reviews, cut onboarding times by 50%, reduce false positives by 70%, and handle 7x more work with the same staff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ComplyAdvantage is headquartered in London and has global hubs in New York, Lisbon, Singapore, and Cluj-Napoca. It is backed by Balderton Capital, Index Ventures, Ontario Teachers’ Pension Plan, Goldman Sachs, and Andreessen Horowitz. Learn more about compliance re-engineered for the age of AI at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://complyadvantage.com&quot;&gt;complyadvantage.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;","departments":[{"id":4044837002,"name":"Commercial","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4024097002,"name":"London, UK","location":"London, England, United Kingdom","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app2.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8785705002/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://complyadvantage.com/careers/jobs/8782207002?gh_jid=8782207002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":6513360002,"location":{"name":"London, England, United Kingdom"},"metadata":null,"id":8782207002,"updated_at":"2026-11-05T08:55:57-05:00","requisition_id":"206170","title":"Product Marketing Lead - Risk Applications ","company_name":"ComplyAdvantage","first_published":"2026-09-03T12:43:03-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Product Marketing Lead to own product marketing for our Risk Applications and Enabling Services portfolio, the products our customers depend on for AML screening, transaction monitoring, payment screening, fraud detection, case management, and regulatory reporting. This is the largest and most active half of our product portfolio, with new products and features shipping continuously. You&#39;ll take ownership of each product wherever it is in its lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the VP of Product Marketing and be one of two Product Marketing Leads building out a newly-forming function. This is a foundational hire, with real latitude to shape how product marketing operates at ComplyAdvantage. You will partner closely with the Product Director who owns this portfolio, translating a steady stream of product and feature launches into positioning, enablement and go-to-market execution that Sales and Customer Success actually use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We run a structured, phased launch process that&#39;s still evolving and you&#39;ll help shape it as you go, deciding what&#39;s genuinely differentiated and worth a moment, and what ships quietly as a release note.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role has no direct reports today. It is a hands-on, individual-contributor role for someone who wants to own outcomes end to end rather than manage other people&#39;s output; someone who can take ambiguous input from Product and Sales and turn it into sharp positioning and a launch that lands, without needing a team underneath them to get there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own product marketing for Risk Applications &amp;amp; Enabling Services. You are responsible for positioning, messaging, launch execution and enablement for this portfolio, end to end, from early roadmap conversations through GA and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Take ownership of products at every stage. Some products in this portfolio are newly launched or launching soon; you&#39;ll pick up their ongoing positioning, enablement and buyer narrative rather than starting from a blank page, and build out what&#39;s missing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead launches end to end. Decide what earns a flagship moment versus what ships quietly, and own the launch plan, messaging and positioning brief for the releases that matter most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the enablement Sales actually uses. Sales decks, demos, battlecards and FAQs written from a real understanding of the buyer and competitive landscape, not templated from a brief.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to competitive intelligence and win-loss. This is shared across the Product Marketing team for now; you&#39;ll help build the muscle until we have dedicated coverage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Represent UK/EMEA (and APAC in the interim) market context. You&#39;re the voice of our primary market in company positioning, even as we build out dedicated regional coverage over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with Product without owning their roadmap. You influence priorities through evidence, buyer feedback, competitive dynamics, win-loss signal, not through authority. You operate as a peer to a Product Director, not a downstream recipient of their decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use AI in your own work. We expect Product Marketing to use AI-assisted workflows for research synthesis, competitive analysis, and first-draft positioning and content. This is how we work, not an aspiration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Essential:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7-10 years of overall professional experience, including 3-5+ years in product marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a high-growth, multi-product technology company; you understand what it means to market a portfolio, not a single product, and to prioritize across competing launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own a launch end to end: positioning, sales enablement, messaging and go-to-market, without heavy oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong independence and autonomy: comfortable defining your own plan within a broader strategy rather than waiting for detailed direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence without authority: you can shape a Product Director&#39;s or sales leader&#39;s thinking through evidence and argument, not reporting lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication: able to translate complex, technical product capability into a sharp, buyer-relevant narrative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a regulated, technical B2B environment, translating product and engineering input into content a commercial audience can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable AI adoption in your own working practice; already using it to work differently, not just interested in it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Preferred:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, security, or identity markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing AI or agentic tools, platforms, or features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing to multiple distinct buyer personas within the same portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with win-loss and competitive intelligence practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Sales on enterprise or upmarket motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At 60 days: You understand the Risk Applications and Enabling Services portfolio end to end, including any products that have recently launched or are approaching launch, and where our competitive and buyer knowledge has gaps. You&#39;ve built working relationships with the Product Director for this portfolio, Sales leadership and Customer Success, and can articulate what&#39;s differentiated in our portfolio and why it matters to a buyer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At 4 months: You are running launches independently through the tiered model. Your highest-priority products have positioning and a sales narrative that Sales trusts and uses, and your enablement materials are the ones reps actually reach for. You&#39;ve built a first cut of the win-loss picture for your portfolio and can speak to it with data, not anecdote.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At 8 months: Your portfolio&#39;s go-to-market motion is measurably working; Sales can point to deals your positioning and enablement helped win. You&#39;re a trusted, senior voice in cross-functional planning for this portfolio, and you&#39;re operating at a level that could reasonably take on more scope as the team grows.&lt;/p&gt;
